     "h": "Raat ka safar, Buraq, panch namazein, aur ‘jism aur rooh ke saath’",
     "t": "Ayah 1: Paak hai woh Zaat jo apne bande ko raat ke ek hisse mein Masjid al-Haram se Masjid al-Aqsa tak le gayi, jis ke gird-o-nawah ko Humne barakat di, taake use apni kuch nishaniyan dikhaye; beshak woh sunne wala, dekhne wala hai. Ibn Kathir (‘The Isra' (Night Journey)’): Allah apni us qudrat ki tasbeeh karta hai jo uske siwa kisi ke paas nahi; ‘bande’ se Muhammad ﷺ, ‘raat mein’ yaani raat ke andhere mein, ‘Masjid al-Haram’ se Makkah ki masjid, aur ‘Masjid al-Aqsa’ se Bayt al-Maqdis (Jerusalem) murad hai jo Ibrahim Khalil ke zamane se Anbiya ka markaz raha; Ibn Kathir ke mutabiq wahan Anbiya jama hue aur Nabi ﷺ ne unhein namaz padhayi (is bayan ki sanad is hisse mein nahi padhi). ‘Barakat’ ka matlab Ibn Kathir ne wahan ki paidawar aur phal kaha, aur ‘nishaniyan’ ke liye 53:18 ka hawala diya. (‘Ahadeeth about Al-Isra'’) mein Ibn Kathir ne kai Sahaba ki riwayaten naql kin. (‘The Report of Anas bin Malik’), jo Ahmad ne record ki: Buraq ek safed janwar tha, gadhe se bada aur khachchar se chhota, jo apni nazar ki intiha par qadam rakhta; Nabi ﷺ Bayt al-Maqdis pahunche, wahan do rakat padhi, phir Jibril ne sharab aur doodh ke do bartan pesh kiye aur Nabi ﷺ ne doodh chuna; Jibril ne kaha ‘aap ne fitrah ko chuna’; phir aasmanon par charhna, har aasman par darwaza khulwana, aur pehle aasman par Adam se mulaqat. Panch namazon ki riwayat: (‘The Report of Anas from Abu Dharr’) mein Ibn Kathir ne Bukhari ki riwayat likhi ke Allah ne pehle pachaas namazein farz kin, Musa ke mashware par Nabi ﷺ baar-baar wapas gaye aur sankhya kam hoti gayi, aakhir mein farmaya gaya ‘yeh paanch hain aur (ajr mein) pachaas hain, mere qaul mein tabdeeli nahi’. Yeh hadith Sahih al-Bukhari 349 (Abu Dharr; sunnah.com par dekhi gayi, ‘Kitab as-Salat: Isra ki raat namaz kaise farz hui’ ke baab mein) hai. Ibn Kathir ne Ibn Mas‘ud ki ek aur riwayat ka bhi zikr kiya jis mein Nabi ﷺ ko paanch namazein, Surah Al-Baqarah ki aakhri ayaten aur shirk na karne walon ke bade gunahon ki maafi di gayi, aur kaha ke yeh Muslim ne record ki (number Story Mode mein verify nahi kiya gaya). (‘The Report of Jabir bin 'Abdullah’): jab Quraysh ne Isra ko jhutlaya to Nabi ﷺ Hijr mein khade hue aur Allah ne Bayt al-Maqdis unke saamne kar diya aur woh use dekh kar uski nishaniyan batate gaye; Ibn Kathir ne kaha yeh Do Sahihon mein bhi hai (number verify nahi). (‘The Report of Abu Hurayrah’): Bukhari aur Muslim ki riwayat mein doodh aur sharab ke do bartan the, Nabi ﷺ ne doodh liya to kaha gaya ‘aap ko fitrah ki hidayat di gayi; agar sharab lete to aapki ummat gumrah ho jati’ (number verify nahi). (‘The Time that Isra' took place, and the Fact that it included both Body and Soul, when the Prophet (ﷺ) was awake, not in a Dream’): Ibn Kathir ke mutabiq Musa bin ‘Uqbah ne Az-Zuhri se naql kiya ke Isra Hijrat se ek saal pehle hua (‘Urwah ka bhi yahi qaul), jabke As-Suddi ne solah mahine pehle kaha; Ibn Kathir ne kaha ke sahih baat yeh hai ke Nabi ﷺ ko jaagte hue, Buraq par Makkah se Bayt al-Maqdis le jaya gaya, phir Mi‘raj (aasmanon par charhne ki seedhi) se saat aasmanon tak, aur yeh khwab nahi tha, kyunke khwab hota to Quraysh itni jaldi jhootha na kehte. Ibn Kathir ne yeh bhi likha ke yeh riwayaten mutawatir hain aur kai Sahaba (‘Umar, ‘Ali, Ibn Mas‘ud, Abu Dharr, Malik bin Sa‘sa‘ah, Abu Hurayrah, Ibn ‘Abbas aur doosre) se aayi hain; kuch riwayaton ke Sahih hone ki shartein poori na hon, tab bhi Musalmanon ka Isra ke hone par ijma hai. (‘An Interesting Story’): Heraclius aur Abu Sufyan ke saath ek waqia Dala'il an-Nubuwwah (Abu Nu‘aym) ke hawale se likha gaya hai; uska poora matn Story Mode mein poora nahi padha. Isra aur Mi‘raj ki baaqi bohat si tafseelaat (jaise Jabir, Ibn ‘Abbas, Ibn Mas‘ud ki riwayaton ka poora matn) bhi Story Mode mein poori nahi padhi gayi."
