     "h": "Namaz ke waqt, aur Fajr ke waqt farishton ki hazri",
     "t": "Ayah 78: suraj dhalne se raat ke andhere tak namaz qaim karo, aur Fajr ka Quran (padhna); beshak Fajr ka Quran (padhna) gawahi diya jata hai. Ibn Kathir (‘The Command to offer the Prayers at their appointed Times’): Allah Nabi ﷺ ko mukarrar waqton par farz namazein padhne ka hukm deta hai. (‘The Meeting of the Angels at the Times of Fajr and 'Asr Prayers’): Ibn Kathir ne At-Tirmidhi, An-Nasa'i aur Ibn Majah ki ek hadith likhi jis mein Fajr ki tilawat par raat aur din ke farishton ki hazri ka zikr hai (At-Tirmidhi ne ‘Hasan Sahih’ kaha), aur Do Sahihon ki Abu Hurayrah ki yeh riwayat: ‘raat aur din ke farishte baari baari tumhare paas aate hain aur Fajr aur Asr ki namaz mein jama hote hain; phir jo tumhare paas raat guzaar kar gaye woh upar jate hain to unka Rabb unse poochhta hai, halaanke woh khud behtar jaanta hai, ‘tum ne mere bandon ko kis haal mein chhoda?’ woh kehte hain ‘hum ne unhein is haal mein chhoda ke woh namaz padh rahe the aur unke paas gaye to bhi namaz padh rahe the’ (number Story Mode mein verify nahi kiya gaya). Ibn Kathir ne Bukhari ki Abu Hurayrah wali ek aur hadith bhi likhi: jamaat ki namaz akele namaz se paccheesh darje behtar hai aur raat-din ke farishte Fajr ki namaz mein jama hote hain; Abu Hurayrah ne kaha ‘chaho to padho: aur Fajr ka Quran padho, beshak Fajr ka Quran gawahi diya jata hai’ (iska number verify nahi). Ibn Mas‘ud ne kaha ke raat aur din ke dono nigehbaan Fajr ki namaz mein milte hain; Ibrahim An-Nakha‘i, Mujahid aur Qatadah ne bhi yahi tafseer ki. Namaz ke har waqt ki tafseeli tashreeh Story Mode mein is entry ke mufassal hisse ke saath poori nahi padhi gayi."
