     "t": "Ayah 85: aur woh tum se rooh ke baare mein poochhte hain; keh do ‘rooh mere Rabb ke amr (hukm) mein se hai, aur tumhein ilm mein se bahut thoda hi diya gaya hai’. Ibn Kathir (‘The Ruh (spirit)’): Ibn Kathir ne Bukhari ki apni Tafsir ki riwayat likhi: ‘Abdullah (Ibn Mas‘ud) ne kaha ke main Nabi ﷺ ke saath ek kheti mein chal raha tha aur aap khajoor ki daali par tek lagaye hue the; kuch Yahudi guzre aur ek ne doosre se kaha ‘inse rooh ke baare mein poocho’; kuch ne kaha ‘kyun poochhte ho, kahin aisa jawab na de jo tumhein napasand ho’, magar unhon ne kaha ‘poocho’; to unhon ne rooh ke baare mein poochha; Nabi ﷺ khamosh rahe aur jawab nahi diya; Ibn Mas‘ud kehte hain ‘main jaan gaya ke aap par wahy aa rahi hai, to main apni jagah par raha’; jab wahy poori hui to Nabi ﷺ ne yeh ayah padhi. Yeh Sahih al-Bukhari 4721 hai (sunnah.com par dekhi gayi; Tafsir 17:85 ke baab mein). Ibn Kathir ne likha ke is riwayat se lagta hai ke yeh ayah Madinah mein utri (jabke Surah Makki hai), aur ek aur riwayat likhi: Ibn Jarir ki ‘Ikrimah ki riwayat ke mutabiq Ahl-e-Kitab ne Nabi ﷺ se rooh ke baare mein poochha aur Allah ne yeh ayah utari; unhon ne kaha ‘aap kehte hain ke humein thoda ilm diya gaya halaanke humein Tawrah mili hai jo Hikmat hai’. Ibn ‘Abbas (Al-‘Awfi ke zariye) ke mutabiq Yahood ne kaha ‘humein rooh ke baare mein batao aur jism mein rooh ko azaab kaise hoga’, Nabi ﷺ ne jawab nahi diya, phir Jibril aaye aur ayah utri, unhon ne poochha ‘kisne bataya?’ Nabi ﷺ ne kaha ‘Jibril Allah ki taraf se laye’, unhon ne kaha ‘Jibril to hamara dushman hai’. (‘The Ruh and the Nafs’): Ibn Kathir ka nichod: rooh asal aur jauhar hai, aur nafs rooh aur uske jism se taalluq ka majmua hai; ek ma‘na mein dono ek hain aur ek mein alag; Ibn Kathir ne kaha ke rooh ki haqeeqat par logon ne bahut bahes ki aur kitabein likhi, aur behtareen mein Al-Hafiz Ibn Mandah ki kitab hai. Rooh ki kaifiyat ke tafseeli masail ke liye Story Mode ka bayan kaafi nahi; ahl-e-ilm se rujoo karein."
